1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,640
What did Ibn al-Qayyim do when he fell ill in Makkah

2
00:00:02,890 --> 00:00:04,880
and could find no doctor and no medicine?

3
00:00:05,650 --> 00:00:08,400
Imam Ibn al-Qayyim (may Allah have mercy on him) recounts in Zad al-Ma‘ad

4
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:09,590
his own personal experience.

5
00:00:10,190 --> 00:00:12,140
He went through a time in Makkah in which he fell ill

6
00:00:12,580 --> 00:00:14,170
and had neither doctor nor medicine.

7
00:00:15,010 --> 00:00:16,600
So he treated himself with al-Fatihah:

8
00:00:16,870 --> 00:00:18,560
he would take a drink of Zamzam water,

9
00:00:18,820 --> 00:00:21,520
recite al-Fatihah over it several times, then drink it.

10
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:22,400
He says:

11
00:00:22,750 --> 00:00:24,370
“I found complete recovery through it.

12
00:00:24,830 --> 00:00:27,670
Then I came to rely on it for many kinds of pain,

13
00:00:27,940 --> 00:00:29,800
and I benefited from it greatly.”

14
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:33,800
This is the experience of a great scholar when all means were cut off from him.

15
00:00:34,220 --> 00:00:36,450
It does not mean we should abandon the doctor when one is available.

16
00:00:36,990 --> 00:00:38,740
So combine al-Fatihah with treatment,

17
00:00:38,940 --> 00:00:41,510
and say as the Prophet (peace be upon him) said:

18
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:44,760
“Allah has not sent down a disease except that He sent down a cure for it.”

19
00:00:45,270 --> 00:00:48,320
Share this story with someone you love, and follow the channel.

